## Wave Execution

<!-- agents-system-setup:wave-execution -->

- For independent work, the orchestrator must **fan out** all parallel-safe subagents in the current wave, wait for all results, synthesize, then start the next wave.
- Sequential delegation is only for overlapping owned paths, direct dependencies, shared-state writes, or approval gates that must complete first.
- Codex uses this root `AGENTS.md` section as its orchestrator guidance; specialized Codex workers stay in `.codex/agents/*.toml`.
- Gemini keeps this policy canonical here and mirrors only root-session notes in `GEMINI.md`.

